-- Basics of Web Designing | Mid 1 | medium | TestId 440009353102015 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440009353102015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A student must apply how the internet and world wide web relate in a practical situation such as a browser requesting a webpage from a remote server. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply website, webpage, web server, domain name and ip address in a practical situation such as opening example.com by typing its domain in a browser. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply purpose of http, https, ftp and tcp/ip in a practical situation such as choosing a protocol for a login page or transferring a file. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply structure of an html5 document in a practical situation such as creating a valid page with a title and visible paragraph. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nThe Internet is the global network of interconnected networks that communicate using Internet protocols, especially the TCP/IP suite. The World Wide Web is one service that operates over the Internet. Web resources are identified with URLs and commonly transferred using HTTP or HTTPS. A browser sends a request, a web server processes it and returns a response. Other Internet services, such as email and file transfer, are not the same as the Web. A clear answer should distinguish the underlying network from the web pages and linked resources delivered through it.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA webpage is one web document; a website is a collection of related pages and resources. A web server is software or a computer that responds to web requests. A domain name is a human-readable name, while an IP address identifies a network endpoint. DNS resolves a domain name to relevant IP address information. The browser then contacts the server using the appropriate protocol and requests the resource. The concepts are related but are not interchangeable: a domain is not the webpage, and a server is not the IP address.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nHTTP transfers web requests and responses; HTTPS uses HTTP over TLS to protect confidentiality and authenticate the server when correctly configured. FTP is designed for file transfer, though secure alternatives are preferred on untrusted networks. TCP provides reliable, ordered delivery, while UDP is connectionless and does not itself guarantee delivery. IP addresses and routes support packet delivery between networks. The protocol should be selected for the task and its security requirements; HTTPS does not repair insecure application logic, and UDP is not a substitute for reliable transport where loss is unacceptable.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA basic HTML5 document starts with `<!DOCTYPE html>`, followed by the `html` root element. The `head` contains metadata such as the character set and the document `title`; the `body` contains the content displayed in the page. Elements use tags and may have attributes. Correct nesting and closing of non-void elements make the document easier to parse and maintain. A suitable page should declare its document type, provide a meaningful title, include required metadata, and place visible content inside the body.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

