ntrol. Which HTML approach fits best?"'::jsonb, '"A CSS rule `.notice { color: red; }` is applied to `<p class=\"notice\">`. What does the selector target?"'::jsonb, '"A browser sends web requests, but the app needs reliable, ordered delivery for the data. Which transport is typically appropriate?"'::jsonb, '"A survey allows a user to select several interests independently. Which control is usually appropriate?"'::jsonb, '"A webpage should animate an element while respecting a design that avoids sudden motion for users who request reduced motion. Which approach is best?"'::jsonb, '"A real-time service prefers low overhead and can tolerate some packet loss without waiting for retransmission. Which transport may fit?"'::jsonb, '"A form submits login details over an unencrypted HTTP connection. What is the primary risk?"'::jsonb, '"A developer serves the same HTML document over HTTP and HTTPS. What does the HTTPS version add when configured correctly?"'::jsonb, '"A small animation should progress through defined stages over time. Which CSS feature is appropriate?"'::jsonb, '"Which distinction between margin and padding is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A title is styled by `h1 { color: black; }` and `.hero { color: teal; }`, and the title has class hero. Assuming equal origin and no !important, which colour applies?"'::jsonb, '"A user enters example.com and receives the matching IP address before connecting to the site. Which service most directly performs this name resolution?"'::jsonb, '"A page must link to a full external website. Which href is generally unambiguous?"'::jsonb, '"A navigation menu should remain positioned relative to its normal place, with a small offset. Which positioning mode best fits?"'::jsonb, '"A website uses a numeric IPv4 address and a newer 128-bit IPv6 address. Which statement is correct?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"href=\"menu\""'::jsonb, '"id=\"menu\""'::jsonb, '"name=\".menu\""'::jsonb, '"class=\"#menu\""'::jsonb, '"Every page automatically gets a