VALUES (4409191201030117, ARRAY['"Choose the correct verb: “Each of the laboratory computers ___ a separate asset number.”"'::jsonb, '"A passage states that a new bus route cut a journey from 50 minutes to 35 minutes. What is the decrease in travel time?"'::jsonb, '"A listener asks for clarification during a presentation. What is the most effective response?"'::jsonb, '"Select the sentence with correct subject–verb agreement."'::jsonb, '"An event report must distinguish facts from opinion. Which entry is a verifiable fact?"'::jsonb, '"Which sentence avoids a dangling modifier?"'::jsonb, '"An email asks for a reply by 4 p.m. and includes three optional background links. Which detail should the recipient note first to act appropriately?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the correct relative pronoun: “The technician ___ repaired the monitor is here.”"'::jsonb, '"Which revision is most concise and formal?"'::jsonb, '"An event report includes time, venue, agenda, attendance and outcomes, but omits the writer''s unsupported claim that the event was ''perfect''. What is the main benefit?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the sentence that expresses a condition correctly."'::jsonb, '"A report states, “The number of visitors rose from 120 to 150.” What was the numerical increase?"'::jsonb, '"The audience cannot hear the last row during a presentation. What should the speaker adjust first?"'::jsonb, '"A speaker has only 90 seconds to explain a process with six steps. What should they do?"'::jsonb, '"Select the sentence with correct parallel structure."'::jsonb, '"Choose the correct passive sentence for “The staff will publish the timetable tomorrow.”"'::jsonb, '"A presenter notices the audience looking confused after a technical definition. What is a useful immediate response?"'::jsonb, '"Which sentence is most appropriate in a formal request email?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement is the strongest closing for a recommendation presentation?"'::jsonb, '"A passage says “Some students prefer printed notes, while others revise using digital files.” Which inference is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"An application needs a clear purpose and the dates requested. Which opening is best?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the sentence in which the modal expresses obligation rather than possibility."'::jsonb, '"A report describes a student event held yesterday. Which tense is best for completed activities?"'::jsonb, '"During Q&A, a question has two parts. What response technique helps avoid missing one part?"'::jsonb, '"Which note-taking method best helps prepare a short summary from a longer article?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the correct verb form: “Neither the students nor the lab assistant ___ available.”"'::jsonb, '"Choose the correct form: “The list of participants, along with the instructor, ___ on the desk.”"'::jsonb, '"A presenter uses highly technical terms with a mixed audience. What is the strongest adjustment?"'::jsonb, '"Choose the correct modal: “You ___ save a backup before changing the system files.”"'::jsonb, '"An article presents a claim and then gives two examples. What is the best reading approach to evaluate whether the examples support the claim?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"has"'::jsonb, '"are having"'::jsonb, '"have"'::jsonb, '"were have"'::jsonb, '"15 minutes"'::jsonb, '"25 minutes"'::jsonb, '"10 minutes"'::jsonb, '"20 minutes"'::jsonb, '"Ignore the question until the end"'::jsonb, '"Pause, restate the point in simpler words, and check whether it is clear"'::jsonb, '"Tell the audience the question is irrelevant"'::jsonb, '"Repeat the same sentence more loudly without checking understanding"'::jsonb, '"The quality of these components are high."'::jsonb, '"The quality of these components have high."'::jsonb, '"The quality of these components were high."'::jsonb, '"The quality of these components is high."'::jsonb, '"The event was the best in college history."'::jsonb, '"Everyone loved every speech."'::jsonb, '"The decorations were unquestionably perfect."'::jsonb, '"The seminar began at 10 a.m. and had 85 registered attendees."'::jsonb, '"Walking into the lab, I noticed the bright lights."'::jsonb, '"Walking into the lab, the lights looked bright."'::jsonb, '"Walking into the lab, the bright lights were noticed."'::jsonb, '"The lights, walking into the lab, looked bright."'::jsonb, '"The length of the signature"'::jsonb, '"The sender''s font choice"'::jsonb, '"The deadline for replying"'::jsonb, '"The number of links only"'::jsonb, '"which"'::jsonb, '"where"'::jsonb, '"whose only"'::jsonb, '"who"'::jsonb, '"The request review, it is taking place."'::jsonb, '"At this point in time, we are currently reviewing the request."'::jsonb, '"We are doing a review of the request at the present time now."'::jsonb, '"We are reviewing the request."'::jsonb, '"It makes the report impossible to read"'::jsonb, '"It prioritizes verifiable reporting over subjective praise"'::jsonb, '"It removes all useful detail"'::jsonb, '"It converts the report into an informal message"'::jsonb, '"If the file will save, we can closed it."'::jsonb, '"If the file saved, we can closes."'::jsonb, '"If the file is saved, we can close the program."'::jsonb, '"If saved the file, we can closing."'::jsonb, '"25"'::jsonb, '"20"'::jsonb, '"30"'::jsonb, '"35"'::jsonb, '"Project the voice clearly toward the audience and check audibility"'::jsonb, '"Remove the microphone without checking"'::jsonb, '"Turn toward the screen and speak into it"'::jsonb, '"Speak faster"'::jsonb, '"Group related steps, highlight key actions, and leave time for a brief summary"'::jsonb, '"Skip the objective and repeat the title"'::jsonb, '"Show a dense slide and remain silent"'::jsonb, '"Read every detail at maximum speed"'::jsonb, '"The role requires planning, testing and documenting results."'::jsonb, '"The role requires to plan, testing and documentation."'::jsonb, '"The role requires planning, testing and to document results."'::jsonb, '"The role requires planning, to test and documentation results."'::jsonb, '"The timetable is publish tomorrow."'::jsonb, '"The timetable has publish tomorrow."'::jsonb, '"The timetable will be published tomorrow."'::jsonb, '"The staff will be published the timetable."'::jsonb, '"Blame the audience"'::jsonb, '"Repeat the definition word-for-word and move on"'::jsonb, '"Give a short example or analogy and invite a clarification question"'::jsonb, '"Proceed faster"'::jsonb, '"I''d be grateful if you could approve the attached plan by Friday."'::jsonb, '"Approval or whatever is fine."'::jsonb, '"You must do it because I said so."'::jsonb, '"Send me the approval today."'::jsonb, '"The topic is complicated, so no decision is possible."'::jsonb, '"To conclude, the trial met the stated criteria; I recommend a monitored rollout and review after one month."'::jsonb, '"That is all, and I do not know what to add."'::jsonb, '"My slides are finished."'::jsonb, '"Printed notes always produce better marks."'::jsonb, '"Students may use different revision preferences."'::jsonb, '"Digital files cannot contain notes."'::jsonb, '"All students dislike digital files."'::jsonb, '"You know why I am writing."'::jsonb, '"I request leave from 14 to 16 December because of a scheduled medical appointment."'::jsonb, '"This is about something I need."'::jsonb, '"Hey, I won''t be there."'::jsonb, '"The file might be corrupted."'::jsonb, '"The upload could finish soon."'::jsonb, '"Users must log out before maintenance."'::jsonb, '"The server may restart tonight."'::jsonb, '"Present continuous only"'::jsonb, '"Future perfect only"'::jsonb, '"Simple past"'::jsonb, '"Simple future"'::jsonb, '"Ask the audience to leave"'::jsonb, '"Briefly restate the two parts, answer each in turn, and check if anything remains"'::jsonb, '"Change to an unrelated slide"'::jsonb, '"Answer only the easiest part"'::jsonb, '"Write only unfamiliar words"'::jsonb, '"Record the main claim and its most relevant supporting points"'::jsonb, '"Record page numbers but no ideas"'::jsonb, '"Copy every sentence without selection"'::jsonb, '"have"'::jsonb, '"is"'::jsonb, '"are"'::jsonb, '"were"'::jsonb, '"have"'::jsonb, '"were"'::jsonb, '"are"'::jsonb, '"is"'::jsonb, '"Keep every term unexplained"'::jsonb, '"Remove all examples"'::jsonb, '"Increase speaking speed"'::jsonb, '"Define essential terms briefly and use examples at the audience''s level"'::jsonb, '"would to"'::jsonb, '"can to"'::jsonb, '"might not have"'::jsonb, '"ought to"'::jsonb, '"Identify the claim and compare each example with it"'::jsonb, '"Assume every example proves the claim"'::jsonb, '"Count the number of paragraphs only"'::jsonb, '"Copy the title without reading"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Communication Skills-I | ESE | medium | TestId 4409191201030129 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4409191201030129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A student must apply planning and writing a clear formal email in a practical situation such as requesting a meeting with a faculty member about a lab submission. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply structure and tone of a formal application in a practical situation such as applying for permission to attend an academic event. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply writing an event or industrial-visit report in a practical situation such as reporting a college visit with observations and outcomes. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply planning and organizing an assignment in a practical situation such as turning a broad topic into a well-structured short assignment. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nA formal email needs a specific subject line, an appropriate greeting, a concise opening that states the purpose, organized details, a clear request or next step, a courteous closing and the sender''s name. Use a professional tone, correct grammar and paragraphs that each serve one purpose. Check the recipient address and any attachment before sending. Add CC only for people who need visibility and BCC when recipients should not see one another''s addresses. Do not place confidential information in unnecessary recipients or subject lines.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA formal application identifies the recipient, date, subject and applicant, then states the request clearly and gives only relevant reasons or supporting details. It uses a respectful salutation, concise body paragraphs, a clear closing and the required signature or identification. The writer should maintain a formal tone, avoid slang and emotional exaggeration, and ensure the requested action is explicit. Proofread names, dates and attachments. A good application lets the recipient understand what is being requested, why it is justified and what response or approval is needed.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA report records an event objectively and in a structured order. Include a meaningful title, date and place, purpose, participants, major activities, observations, outcomes and a conclusion or recommendations where appropriate. Arrange events chronologically or under clear headings and use past tense for completed activities. Separate observed facts from personal opinion and support claims with reliable details. Proofread names and dates, keep the language concise, and make the report useful to a reader who did not attend the event.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nBegin by interpreting the task and identifying the expected scope. Gather relevant sources, make an outline, and organize the introduction, main discussion and conclusion in a logical sequence. Each paragraph should develop one idea and connect it to the overall argument. Use accurate examples and acknowledge sources in the required format; do not copy text without attribution. Revise for completeness, flow, factual accuracy and grammar, then check formatting and submission requirements. A strong assignment answers the exact question rather than merely collecting loosely related information.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Computer Fundamental Skill | Mid 1 | medium | TestId 440009352101015 | mcq
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440009352101015, ARRAY['"Which action changes a folder''s name without changing its contents?"'::jsonb, '"Which HTML element inserts an image when a valid source is supplied?"'::jsonb, '"Which software manages hardware resources and services for applications?"'::jsonb, '"Windows is to be installed on a laptop containing irreplaceable files. What should be done before changing partitions?"'::jsonb, '"A Linux command must list files, then enter a directory named reports. Which sequence fits?"'::jsonb, '"What is the usual purpose of BIOS/firmware during startup?"'::jsonb, '"A computer has no usable display after a resolution change. Which recovery attempt is most appropriate first?"'::jsonb, '"In File Explorer, how can a user select several non-adjacent files?"'::jsonb, '"Which command-line command normally changes the current directory?"'::jsonb, '"A file''s exact location and size must be checked without opening it. Which feature is appropriate?"'::jsonb, '"Which component provides the main connection platform for CPU, memory and expansion devices?"'::jsonb, '"A page should have a background image while keeping a paragraph readable. Which implementation is best?"'::jsonb, '"A Linux user wants to inspect permissions and file details, including hidden entries, before changing access. Which command is safest?"'::jsonb, '"Which device is primarily an input device?"'::jsonb, '"What is a folder used for?"'::jsonb, '"What does copying a file usually do?"'::jsonb, '"A Windows PC is slow after startup. The user wants evidence about resource use before uninstalling software. What is the best first check?"'::jsonb, '"What should a user enter to open a known website directly from the browser address bar?"'::jsonb, '"A user needs detailed file listings including hidden entries in a Unix shell. Which command is best?"'::jsonb, '"A paragraph''s formatting must be reused without copying its text. What is the best tool?"'::jsonb, '"A workstation is shared by several students.