VALUES (4400913511010117, ARRAY['"An object is 125 mm long and drawn at RF 4:1. What drawing length is required?"'::jsonb, '"A drawing measures 60 mm for an actual length of 30 mm. Which scale is used?"'::jsonb, '"An isometric drawing uses true lengths along its axes. How does this differ from isometric projection?"'::jsonb, '"A line''s front and top projections are both shorter than its true length. What does this suggest?"'::jsonb, '"A conic needs to be constructed from focus/directrix information. Which construction family is relevant?"'::jsonb, '"Under first-angle projection, where is the right-side view placed relative to the front view?"'::jsonb, '"A line is inclined to both HP and VP. How should its true length be found from projections?"'::jsonb, '"A point is above HP and behind VP. Which quadrant is it in?"'::jsonb, '"A polygon is parallel to HP. Which view shows its true shape?"'::jsonb, '"Which methods are suitable for constructing a parabola under the syllabus?"'::jsonb, '"A point has zero height above HP and lies in front of VP. Where does it lie?"'::jsonb, '"A cutting plane passes through a hollow block to reveal its cavity. Which view shows the internal arrangement?"'::jsonb, '"A student uses hidden lines for every visible edge. What is the correction?"'::jsonb, '"A tangent and normal are needed at a plotted point. What relationship must hold?"'::jsonb, '"A hyperbola is constructed from focus and directrix information. Which method family applies?"'::jsonb, '"A line has true length 80 mm and is parallel to VP. Which projection shows its true length?"'::jsonb, '"A circle rolls around the outside of a fixed circle. Which curve fits?"'::jsonb, '"An ellipse construction uses two concentric circles. What is the key feature?"'::jsonb, '"A component is 150 mm long. At RF 1:5, how long should it be drawn?"'::jsonb, '"Which arrangement is characteristic of third-angle projection?"'::jsonb, '"A physical length of 2.4 m is represented by 120 mm. What is the RF?"'::jsonb, '"A plane is inclined to HP and its true shape is needed. Which method is appropriate?"'::jsonb, '"A road section is 4.5 km and must fit as 90 mm on a drawing. What RF is required?"'::jsonb, '"A plane lamina is inclined to HP but parallel to VP. Which view shows true shape?"'::jsonb, '"A cycloid is constructed from a rolling circle. What motion generates it?"'::jsonb, '"A circular plane is inclined to HP. Why can its top view appear elliptical?"'::jsonb, '"A line is inclined to HP but parallel to VP. Which view gives its true length and inclination to HP?"'::jsonb, '"For a circle, where is the normal at a point located?"'::jsonb, '"A long object must be represented smaller while actual length remains clear. What information is important?"'::jsonb, '"Which principle distinguishes first-angle from third-angle projection?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"500 mm"'::jsonb, '"125 mm"'::jsonb, '"250 mm"'::jsonb, '"31.25 mm"'::jsonb, '"1:1 full size"'::jsonb, '"1:2 reducing"'::jsonb, '"2:1 enlarging"'::jsonb, '"1:3 reducing"'::jsonb, '"An isometric drawing cannot show three dimensions"'::jsonb, '"Isometric drawing generally uses true lengths; isometric projection uses foreshortened lengths"'::jsonb, '"Isometric projection always uses perspective convergence"'::jsonb, '"Both must use RF 1:1"'::jsonb, '"It lies on both principal planes"'::jsonb, '"It is parallel to both HP and VP"'::jsonb, '"The line is inclined to both HP and VP"'::jsonb, '"The drawing is necessarily wrong"'::jsonb, '"Conic construction"'::jsonb, '"Thread notation"'::jsonb, '"Isometric projection"'::jsonb, '"Cycloid construction"'::jsonb, '"Below the plan only"'::jsonb, '"Left of the front view"'::jsonb, '"Right of the front view"'::jsonb, '"Above the title block"'::jsonb, '"Take the shorter projection as true length"'::jsonb, '"Replace both projections by an isometric scale"'::jsonb, '"Assume either projection equals true length"'::jsonb, '"Use projection construction/auxiliary views or successive rotations as required"'::jsonb, '"Third"'::jsonb, '"Second"'::jsonb, '"Fourth"'::jsonb, '"First"'::jsonb, '"Right-side view always"'::jsonb, '"Front view"'::jsonb, '"Only an isometric drawing"'::jsonb, '"Top view/plan"'::jsonb, '"Concentric-circle ellipse method only"'::jsonb, '"Isometric scale method"'::jsonb, '"Rectangle method or method of tangents (triangle method)"'::jsonb, '"Involute method"'::jsonb, '"On HP and in front of VP"'::jsonb, '"Below HP and behind VP"'::jsonb, '"Above HP and in front of VP"'::jsonb, '"Above HP and behind VP"'::jsonb, '"Sectional view"'::jsonb, '"Scale bar"'::jsonb, '"Centre line only"'::jsonb, '"Unsectioned isometric view only"'::jsonb, '"Use centre lines as outlines"'::jsonb, '"Use continuous thick object lines for visible edges and dashed lines for hidden edges"'::jsonb, '"Use dimensions for every edge"'::jsonb, '"Remove all line distinctions"'::jsonb, '"They meet only at a focus"'::jsonb, '"Both must be centre lines"'::jsonb, '"They are perpendicular at that point"'::jsonb, '"They are parallel"'::jsonb, '"Concentric-circle ellipse method only"'::jsonb, '"Cycloid rolling method"'::jsonb, '"Third-angle projection"'::jsonb, '"Focus-directrix method"'::jsonb, '"Top view on HP only"'::jsonb, '"Title block"'::jsonb, '"Front elevation on VP"'::jsonb, '"Section hatch"'::jsonb, '"Rectangular hyperbola"'::jsonb, '"Epicycloid"'::jsonb, '"Hypocycloid"'::jsonb, '"Cycloid"'::jsonb, '"The method turns all lines into hidden lines"'::jsonb, '"The circles have unrelated centres"'::jsonb, '"The method only constructs a cycloid"'::jsonb, '"Corresponding radial divisions and projected points locate points on the ellipse"'::jsonb, '"750 mm"'::jsonb, '"15 mm"'::jsonb, '"30 mm"'::jsonb, '"75 mm"'::jsonb, '"Plan below front view, right-side view left"'::jsonb, '"Plan below title block regardless of elevation"'::jsonb, '"All views stacked without alignment"'::jsonb, '"Plan above front view, right-side view to the right"'::jsonb, '"1:20"'::jsonb, '"1:200"'::jsonb, '"1:10"'::jsonb, '"2:1"'::jsonb, '"Use hidden lines only"'::jsonb, '"Use an auxiliary plane/view parallel to the lamina or a change-of-plane method"'::jsonb, '"Set every dimension to 1:1"'::jsonb, '"Replace its boundary with a centre line"'::jsonb, '"1:50,000"'::jsonb, '"5:1"'::jsonb, '"1:500,000"'::jsonb, '"1:5,000"'::jsonb, '"Front view on VP"'::jsonb, '"Only the isometric view"'::jsonb, '"Top view on HP"'::jsonb, '"A side view in every case"'::jsonb, '"A point rotating about a fixed centre only"'::jsonb, '"A point on the circle rolling without slipping along a straight line"'::jsonb, '"A cone cut by a plane"'::jsonb, '"A line parallel to the directrix"'::jsonb, '"All circles always draw as ellipses"'::jsonb, '"Projection foreshortens dimensions when the circle is inclined to the projection plane"'::jsonb, '"The real circle changes shape"'::jsonb, '"The scale ratio changes non-uniformly in every view"'::jsonb, '"Title-block view"'::jsonb, '"Top view only"'::jsonb, '"Front elevation"'::jsonb, '"Section hatch"'::jsonb, '"Parallel to every diameter"'::jsonb, '"Along the tangent through the point"'::jsonb, '"On the dimension line"'::jsonb, '"Along the radius through the point of contact"'::jsonb, '"Isometric view without measurements"'::jsonb, '"Omit dimensions because a scale exists"'::jsonb, '"Only line colour"'::jsonb, '"Appropriate RF, clear dimensioning and scale notation"'::jsonb, '"Relative placement of object, observer and projection plane"'::jsonb, '"Number of dimensions shown"'::jsonb, '"Whether colour is used"'::jsonb, '"Number of line types"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Engineering Drawing | ESE | medium | TestId 4400913511010129 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (4400913511010129, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A student must apply drawing instruments, bis conventions, line types and layout in a practical situation such as preparing a standards-based engineering sheet before drawing a component. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply representative fraction and selection of drawing scales in a practical situation such as choosing a scale to fit a large object on a small sheet. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply dimensioning and annotation of engineering drawings in a practical situation such as making a component drawing usable by a workshop without verbal explanation. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply orthographic projection and first-angle versus third-angle methods in a practical situation such as producing front, top and side views from a pictorial object. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nA drawing sheet should have a suitable size, border, title block and layout, with space allocated for views and notes. Instruments such as drawing boards, T-squares or parallel rules, set squares, compass, divider and scale support accurate construction. Standard line conventions distinguish visible outlines, hidden edges, centre lines, dimensions and construction work. Use lettering and dimensioning consistently and choose a suitable scale when the object will not fit at full size. Standards make drawings legible and interpretable by others, rather than relying on informal assumptions.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nRepresentative fraction (RF) is drawing length divided by actual length after both are expressed in the same units. A full-size scale has RF 1:1; a reducing scale has RF below one, and an enlarging scale has RF greater than one. For example, RF 1:5 means a 50 mm actual length is shown as 10 mm on the drawing. Select a scale that preserves legibility and available sheet space, state it clearly, and apply it consistently to dimensions and construction. The written dimension normally states actual size, not the measured paper length.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nDimensioning communicates the size and position of features. Use clear extension and dimension lines, legible figures and appropriate symbols, and avoid repeating dimensions or creating ambiguity. Choose line types according to their purpose: visible outlines, hidden details, centre lines and dimension lines should be distinguishable. Annotations should be placed near the relevant feature without clutter. A drawing should contain enough dimensions to manufacture or inspect the part, but not contradictory or redundant values. Apply the relevant standard conventions and check units and overall dimensions.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nOrthographic projection represents an object through views perpendicular to principal planes. The front view communicates height and width, the top view width and depth, and a side view height and depth. In first-angle projection, the object is between the observer and projection plane; in third-angle projection, the projection plane is between observer and object. Therefore the arrangement of views differs. Identify the projection method by its symbol or stated convention, align corresponding dimensions across views, and check that the set of views describes one consistent object.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Indian Constitution | Mid 1 | medium | TestId 440091210101015 | mcq
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440091210101015, ARRAY['"A citizen damages public property during a protest. Which Fundamental Duty is most directly relevant to the conduct?"'::jsonb, '"A state policy seeks environmental improvement, but an official arbitrarily denies access to a public benefit. What is a balanced analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A constitutional amendment changes the composition of a body, and challengers claim the change damages separation of powers and judicial review. What evidence is most important to the basic-structure question?"'::jsonb, '"Who chaired the Drafting Committee of the Constituent Assembly?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Right is asserted against a policy goal in Part IV. Which reading method best reflects the constitutional relationship?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"India is described in the Preamble as a:"'::jsonb, '"A student says that because the Constitution is written, every rule must appear in one unamended original document. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen challenges an order affecting personal liberty. The authority claims Article 21 only applies when a law is completely absent, not when procedure exists but is arbitrary. Which response best reflects modern constitutional reasoning at course level?"'::jsonb, '"Who is the constitutional head of a state in India?"'::jsonb, '"A claimant argues that because a policy appears in Part IV, courts must enforce it as if it were a Fundamental Right. Which constitutional text most directly challenges that claim?"'::jsonb, '"A government scheme promotes social welfare, but its implementation treats similarly situated citizens arbitrarily. Which constitutional analysis is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"Which part opens the Constitution of India and states its guiding ideals?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment changes an institution in a way alleged to eliminate judicial review and constitutional limits. Which framework most directly addresses whether a constitutional amendment can destroy foundational features?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A student argues that the Preamble itself grants an unlimited legal power to an executive agency. What is the key flaw?"'::jsonb, '"An official says Article 14 guarantees identical treatment even where relevant circumstances differ. Which statement is more accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A teacher is describing an amendment''s constitutional history. Which pair is correct?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article protects specified freedoms, subject to constitutional restrictions?"'::jsonb, '"A person says all Directive Principles are individually enforceable in court because they are ''fundamental in governance''. Which reasoning corrects the conflation?"'::jsonb, '"A school textbook says Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution through an amendment. Which pairing is correct?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article guarantees equality before the law and equal protection of the laws?"'::jsonb, '"When did the Constitution of India come into force?"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution''s Preamble is invoked to interpret an ambiguous provision. Which description best fits its role?"'::jsonb, '"A new state policy is consistent with a Directive Principle but is implemented in a way that violates Article 21. What follows?"'::jsonb, '"What is the principal purpose of a constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A Fundamental Duty to protect the environment is cited to automatically deny a person''s otherwise lawful speech. Which conclusion is most careful?"'::jsonb, '"Which Article protects life and personal liberty?"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights are primarily contained in which Part of the Constitution?"'::jsonb, '"A law restricts a citizen''s speech to address a public concern. The citizen argues Article 19 makes all restrictions invalid. Which reasoning is most defensible?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Assume Fundamental Duties erase all legal procedures"'::jsonb, '"Assume Article 14 applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Treat the environmental aim as an automatic exemption from equality"'::jsonb, '"Recognize the environmental aim and Article 51A duty, while also assessing whether the decision complies with applicable rights such as Article 14"'::jsonb, '"The amendment''s actual legal effects on the alleged foundational features, considered under the basic-structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"How many local wards exist"'::jsonb, '"Whether the amendment uses formal language"'::jsonb, '"Whether a state Governor publicly supports the amendment"'::jsonb, '"Jawaharlal Nehru"'::jsonb, '"B. R. Ambedkar"'::jsonb, '"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel"'::jsonb, '"Rajendra Prasad"'::jsonb, '"Read the provisions harmoniously, recognizing enforceable rights and the directive role of Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Always disregard Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Assume both Parts have identical justiciability"'::jsonb, '"Treat Directive Principles as criminal offences"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 permits no restrictions in any circumstances"'::jsonb, '"Check the relevant freedom and whether the restriction fits a constitutionally permitted ground and is reasonable"'::jsonb, '"Treat Article 19 as a duty rather than a right"'::jsonb, '"Any restriction is automatically unconstitutional"'::jsonb, '"Presidential Kingdom"'::jsonb, '"Sovereign Socialist Secular Democratic Republic"'::jsonb, '"Confederation of Provinces"'::jsonb, '"Federal Monarchy"'::jsonb, '"Written constitutions can be amended according to their prescribed procedures"'::jsonb, '"Written constitutions cannot change"'::jsonb, '"Only Governors can amend the Constitution"'::jsonb, '"Amendments automatically replace all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"Any written procedure automatically validates every deprivation"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 only applies during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 and 21 cannot ever be considered together"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection includes scrutiny of the legal procedure affecting life and liberty; the existence of a procedure alone does not end analysis"'::jsonb, '"Speaker of the Assembly"'::jsonb, '"Governor"'::jsonb, '"District Collector"'::jsonb, '"Chief Minister"'::jsonb, '"Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Article 21"'::jsonb, '"Article 37"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k)"'::jsonb, '"Consider Part IV''s policy objective while separately testing implementation under Article 14 and relevant rights"'::jsonb, '"A welfare purpose removes the need for legal authority"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles automatically excuse unequal treatment"'::jsonb, '"Only Article 324 applies to all government actions"'::jsonb, '"A private affidavit"'::jsonb, '"Preamble"'::jsonb, '"Schedule of office hours"'::jsonb, '"A municipal budget"'::jsonb, '"The basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"The ordinary rule for email notices"'::jsonb, '"The municipal corporation framework"'::jsonb, '"Freedom of speech under Article 19 only"'::jsonb, '"Equality before law and equal protection under Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Election administration under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duty under Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Only the Preamble sets out local election procedures"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble is the same as Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble overrides all operative Articles"'::jsonb, '"The Preamble expresses constitutional values and aids interpretation; it does not independently grant unlimited executive authority"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only concerns local elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 abolishes all classification"'::jsonb, '"Equality requires equal protection and bars arbitrary discrimination, but