VALUES (4400912101010117, ARRAY['"A student confuses the Chief Election Commissioner with the State Election Commissioner. Which distinction is most accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A policy objective appears in Part IV, but a petitioner wants a court order solely to enforce it as a Directive Principle. Which constitutional statement is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"An official detains a person and relies only on a personal preference, without lawful authority or procedure. Which provision is most directly engaged?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen damages public property during a protest. Which Fundamental Duty is most directly relevant to the conduct?"'::jsonb, '"The Prime Minister''s Council of Ministers loses a confidence vote in Lok Sabha. Which constitutional principle is most directly implicated?"'::jsonb, '"A policy objective is listed as a Directive Principle and is consistent with a Fundamental Right. Which approach best reflects the Constitution''s framework?"'::jsonb, '"A person argues that a Fundamental Right can never be limited. Which response best fits the course topics?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment changes a constitutional provision but is challenged for damaging the Constitution''s basic structure. Which doctrine is most relevant?"'::jsonb, '"A bill concerning ordinary Union governance is being studied. Which distinction between Parliament and the executive is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A parent or guardian is asked which Fundamental Duty concerns children''s education. Which is accurate?"'::jsonb, '"A general election to the Lok Sabha is being conducted, and a separate city municipal election is scheduled. Which bodies have the respective constitutional roles?"'::jsonb, '"A policy proposal concerns village-level elected self-government. Which amendment is most directly connected with the Panchayat framework?"'::jsonb, '"A legal complaint concerns both an arbitrary procedure affecting liberty and unequal treatment under law. Which Articles are most directly relevant?"'::jsonb, '"A student says Fundamental Duties and Fundamental Rights are identical because both appear in the Constitution. Which correction is strongest?"'::jsonb, '"An amendment is challenged as destroying a foundational feature such as constitutional supremacy. Which case-law doctrine is relevant to the course''s basic-structure topic?"'::jsonb, '"Which statement best describes the ECI''s constitutional role?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority refuses the same legal protection to two people in materially identical circumstances without a relevant reason. Which constitutional principle is most directly raised?"'::jsonb, '"A Governor receives advice from a state''s Council of Ministers for ordinary state executive business. Which official is the normal political head of that Council?"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution''s Preamble is invoked to interpret an ambiguous provision. Which description best fits its role?"'::jsonb, '"A person argues that the Constitution exists only to empower the government. Which Preamble value most clearly contradicts an unlimited-power view?"'::jsonb, '"A district administration office is implementing state policy and coordinating local public services. Which level is most directly represented?"'::jsonb, '"A district officer administers relief in the district and coordinates local departments. Which syllabus topic is most directly illustrated?"'::jsonb, '"A state makes policy to improve public health and welfare. Which constitutional part is especially relevant as guiding principles for State policy?"'::jsonb, '"A school textbook says Fundamental Duties were added to the Constitution through an amendment. Which pairing is correct?"'::jsonb, '"A municipality''s constitutional framework is being discussed. Which Part was added for urban local bodies by the 74th Amendment?"'::jsonb, '"A State Election Commission plans local-body elections, but a student says Article 324 alone assigns the ECI all elections of every kind. Which correction is best?"'::jsonb, '"A public authority treats people unequally and also restricts a citizen''s speech. Which two provisions are the most direct starting points for analysis?"'::jsonb, '"A local body has been asked to handle city-level services rather than district rural planning. Which institution is a better fit?"'::jsonb, '"A citizen''s speech is restricted by a law. Which is the most accurate way to evaluate the restriction under Article 19?"'::jsonb, '"A government policy promotes public health but a person argues it is a Directive Principle. Which statement best distinguishes its legal status from a Fundamental Right?"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"The Chief Election Commissioner runs municipal elections in each city directly"'::jsonb, '"The ECI handles Parliament and State Legislature elections; State ECs handle Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"The State EC appoints the President"'::jsonb, '"Both are the same officer under all circumstances"'::jsonb, '"All policies in Part IV are criminal provisions"'::jsonb, '"Part IV is the same as Part III"'::jsonb, '"Article 37 states Directive Principles are not enforceable by courts, while remaining fundamental in governance"'::jsonb, '"Part IV applies only during elections"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 protection of life and personal liberty"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 only"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 only in every possible case"'::jsonb, '"Duty to serve as a judge"'::jsonb, '"Duty to vote in every election as stated in Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Duty to protect the environment only"'::jsonb, '"Duty to safeguard public property and abjure violence"'::jsonb, '"Collective responsibility of the Union Council of Ministers to Lok Sabha"'::jsonb, '"The independence of the State Election Commission"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duties under Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"Governor''s appointment power"'::jsonb, '"Treat Directive Principles as automatically unenforceable in every policy decision"'::jsonb, '"Read the provisions harmoniously, recognizing Part IV''s guidance and Part III''s enforceable rights"'::jsonb, '"Use Part IV as the sole source of criminal offences"'::jsonb, '"Ignore all Fundamental Rights"'::jsonb, '"All Fundamental Rights can be cancelled by an ordinary officer"'::jsonb, '"Article 21 applies only to elected legislators"'::jsonb, '"Part III contains only non-binding policy aims"'::jsonb, '"Some rights, including Article 19 freedoms, are subject to constitutionally specified restrictions"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of double taxation only"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of colourable printing"'::jsonb, '"Basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"Principle of absolute parliamentary supremacy"'::jsonb, '"Parliament is the Union legislature; the Council of Ministers is part of the executive"'::jsonb, '"The Governor presides over both Houses of Parliament"'::jsonb, '"The Supreme Court is one of Parliament''s Houses"'::jsonb, '"The Election Commission debates and enacts all laws"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 requires free university education in every case"'::jsonb, '"Article 21A is a Fundamental Duty"'::jsonb, '"Article 51A(k) addresses providing educational opportunities to a child/ward aged 6–14"'::jsonb, '"Article 14 requires every parent to be a teacher"'::jsonb, '"Governor personally conducts both"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation runs both elections"'::jsonb, '"Election Commission of India for Lok Sabha; State Election Commission for municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"State Election Commission conducts both in every case"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"52nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"74th Amendment"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment"'::jsonb, '"Articles 75 and 164"'::jsonb, '"Articles 14 and 21"'::jsonb, '"Articles 51A and 324 only"'::jsonb, '"Articles 243K and 243ZA"'::jsonb, '"Both sets apply only to the President"'::jsonb, '"Duties are found only in local bylaws"'::jsonb, '"Rights are found only in Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Rights are enforceable rights in Part III; Fundamental Duties are listed for citizens in Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"Doctrine of parliamentary privilege only"'::jsonb, '"Local election rotation"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles'' non-justiciability"'::jsonb, '"Basic structure doctrine"'::jsonb, '"It administers all municipal services"'::jsonb, '"It appoints all Governors"'::jsonb, '"It makes all criminal laws"'::jsonb, '"It supervises specified electoral rolls and elections under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Equality before law and equal protection under Article 14"'::jsonb, '"Fundamental Duty under Article 51A only"'::jsonb, '"Election administration under Article 324"'::jsonb, '"Freedom of speech under Article 19 only"'::jsonb, '"Chief Minister"'::jsonb, '"President"'::jsonb, '"Chief Election Commissioner"'::jsonb, '"Lok Sabha Speaker"'::jsonb, '"A source of unrestricted executive power"'::jsonb, '"A useful aid expressing constitutional objectives and values, read with the text rather than replacing it"'::jsonb, '"A separate criminal code replacing all Articles"'::jsonb, '"A local-government regulation"'::jsonb, '"Abolition of judicial review"'::jsonb, '"Unlimited terms for every elected body"'::jsonb, '"Justice, liberty, equality and fraternity as constitutional objectives"'::jsonb, '"Absolute executive discretion"'::jsonb, '"Union Legislature"'::jsonb, '"District administration"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation only in every case"'::jsonb, '"Supreme Court Registry"'::jsonb, '"State election of Rajya Sabha members"'::jsonb, '"District administration"'::jsonb, '"Preamble interpretation only"'::jsonb, '"Union Parliament procedure"'::jsonb, '"Part XV only"'::jsonb, '"Part II"'::jsonb, '"Part IV"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA only"'::jsonb, '"74th Amendment, Article 21"'::jsonb, '"42nd Amendment, Part IVA/Article 51A"'::jsonb, '"44th Amendment, Part II"'::jsonb, '"73rd Amendment, Article 19"'::jsonb, '"Part II"'::jsonb, '"Part IXA"'::jsonb, '"Part III"'::jsonb, '"Part IVA"'::jsonb, '"All elections are conducted by municipal commissioners"'::jsonb, '"Article 324 deals only with school elections"'::jsonb, '"Local elections are not constitutionally addressed"'::jsonb, '"The Constitution separately provides for State Election Commissions for Panchayat and municipal elections"'::jsonb, '"Articles 14 and 19"'::jsonb, '"Articles 51A and 324"'::jsonb, '"Articles 72 and 161 only"'::jsonb, '"Articles 73 and 74 only"'::jsonb, '"Union Council of Ministers"'::jsonb, '"Zila Panchayat"'::jsonb, '"Rajya Sabha"'::jsonb, '"Municipal Corporation"'::jsonb, '"Any restriction is automatically unconstitutional"'::jsonb, '"Article 19 permits no restrictions in any circumstances"'::jsonb, '"Check the relevant freedom and whether the restriction fits a constitutionally permitted ground and is reasonable"'::jsonb, '"Treat Article 19 as a duty rather than a right"'::jsonb, '"A Directive Principle guides state policy but is not directly enforceable in the same way as a Fundamental Right"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles apply only to citizens'' private conduct"'::jsonb, '"Every Directive Principle is an offence provision"'::jsonb, '"Directive Principles always override every Fundamental Right"'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY['1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

-- Mathematics-I | Mid 1 | medium | TestId 440091312101015 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440091312101015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A student must apply number sets and laws of indices in a practical situation such as simplifying a product and quotient of powers with the same non-zero base. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply hcf and lcm of integers in a practical situation such as finding the HCF and LCM of 12 and 18. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply hcf and lcm of fractions and decimals in a practical situation such as finding HCF and LCM for 2/3 and 4/5 after simplifying the fractions. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A student must apply polynomial definitions and arithmetic operations in a practical situation such as simplifying (2x + 3) + (x − 5) and identifying degree. Explain the method or reasoning, set out the main steps, and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer:\nNumber sets include natural numbers, whole numbers, integers, rational numbers, irrational numbers and real numbers, with each set having specific membership rules. For a non-zero base a, powers follow laws such as a^m × a^n = a^(m+n), a^m ÷ a^n = a^(m−n), (a^m)^n = a^(mn), and a^0 = 1. These laws require attention to conditions such as non-zero denominators and the base not being zero for a^0. For example, 2^3 × 2^4 ÷ 2^5 = 2^(3+4−5) = 2^2 = 4.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nThe HCF is the greatest positive integer that divides every given integer; the LCM is the smallest positive common multiple. Prime factorization is a reliable method: 12 = 2^2 × 3 and 18 = 2 × 3^2. For HCF, take common prime factors with the smallest exponents, giving 2 × 3 = 6. For LCM, take each prime factor with the greatest exponent, giving 2^2 × 3^2 = 36. For positive integers, HCF × LCM equals the product of the two integers.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nFirst express fractions in their lowest terms. For positive fractions, the usual course rules are HCF = HCF of numerators divided by LCM of denominators, and LCM = LCM of numerators divided by HCF of denominators. Thus for 2/3 and 4/5, HCF = 2/15 and LCM = 4. For decimals, convert values to integers by multiplying by an appropriate power of ten, find the HCF/LCM, then rescale the result. Keep the decimal-place adjustment consistent and verify the resulting multiples or divisors.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb, '"Model answer:\nA polynomial is an expression formed from constants and variables with non-negative integer exponents and coefficients. Like terms have the same variable part and exponents, so only their coefficients are combined. For example, (2x + 3) + (x − 5) = 3x − 2. The degree of a non-zero polynomial in one variable is the highest exponent with a non-zero coefficient; the degree of 3x^4 − 2x^2 + 7 is four. Keep signs and exponents unchanged while grouping terms, and simplify before identifying the degree.\n\n8-mark marking guide: 2 marks for the core concept; 3 marks for accurate principles, steps or formulas; 2 marks for an example/application; 1 mark for a justified conclusion or check. A strong answer should connect the concept to the stated example, explain the steps in order and justify the outcome."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

